5,"Kham, Eastern Parbate Language (KIF) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kif/,"Eastern Parbate Kham is an endangered indigenous language of Nepal. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Kham, Eastern Parbate",Sino-Tibetan
6,Magar Kham language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Magar_Kham_language,"The Magar Kham language encompasses four primary dialects, each recognized as a distinct variety within the Kham subgroup of the Sino-Tibetan family. These dialects are Gamal Kham, Sheshi Kham, Eastern Parbate Kham, and Western Parbate Kham.","Kham, Eastern Parbate",Sino-Tibetan
